{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 55, :comments ["<b>For the children of Israel are slaves to Me.</b> Above, where it writes ״כי עבדי הם״ — it speaks of one sold to an Israelite, his brother; but if he is sold to a Canaanite, who is of another nation — there is no concern, as established below."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "סד״א appears to be an abbreviation for סוף דבר אחר, 'end of another matter,' i.e., a cross-reference to what follows; קמ״ל = קא מפרש לקמן, 'it is explained below.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:21.681793347Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}